Tournament Analysis over Poincare/symmetry proof carriers
  score_hist=[(0, 1), (1, 1), (2, 1), (3, 1), (4, 1), (5, 1), (6, 1), (7, 1)]
  directed_3cycles=0
  hamiltonian_path=individual_sign_flip_parity_kernel > observer_coupled_worldline_tube_groupoid > integer_time_dilation_primitive_scale > anchored_metric_winding_tournament > stationary_velocity_translation > bare_winding_iso_class > lorentz_velocity_addition_shadow > raw_speed_scalar

Carrier guardrails
  individual_sign_flip_parity_kernel         destroyed=pairwise winding orientation and tournament order
  observer_coupled_worldline_tube_groupoid   destroyed=none if observer worldline and tube metric are retained
  integer_time_dilation_primitive_scale      destroyed=raw magnitude before primitive/gcd normalization
  anchored_metric_winding_tournament         destroyed=continuous tube widths unless threshold gaps are attached
  stationary_velocity_translation            destroyed=observer velocity; not a standard LRC automorphism
  bare_winding_iso_class                     destroyed=metric gap widths, observer placement, exact Farey scale
  lorentz_velocity_addition_shadow           destroyed=integer-speed lattice and fixed Euclidean circle metric
  raw_speed_scalar                           destroyed=everything packet-level

Proof-target readout
  True automorphisms for the standard anchored LRC predicate:
    runner permutation, independent sign flips, global reflection, integer dilation/primitive scaling.
  Observer-coupled boosts are exact only in the enlarged worldline groupoid:
    keep observer velocity, then recenter by relative speeds.
  Stationary velocity translation is the useful failure mode:
    it measures exactly why observer labels cannot be quotiented away.
  Lorentz/Poincare language should enter as a cone/tube ledger, not a speed scalar:
    if a boost tilts the danger tube, the metric, observer, and lattice labels become load-bearing.
